      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "Hi Anna. Yulia and I are working on changes to the Customize sidebar panel and one of the changes we'd like to make is to add a tooltip to one of the checkbox options. The checkbox is not checked by default and is - of course - optional to check. The information we want to include in the tooltip is not essential, we think, to the user in understanding the option (based on user testing, users understand the string) but is more of an addendum for users who are interested in the option, explaining how they can show tabs. \n\nWe also explored doing a callout for users who choose this option, to share the same information. But, have received feedback from engineering that the callout would be more work - so, something we might not have capacity to do. \n\nDo you have any concerns here from an accessibility perspective with using a tooltip?  \n@Anna Yeddi cc: @Yulia Popova",
